A||N||7||GT-maniac||Dead motor||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||08-12-2000||12:42 PM||||The motor in my GT is now seized. Something to do with the oil filter falling off the motor and all the oil being pumped out before I could stop the car. My question is what would be cheaper rebuilding the 2.8 with stock parts or buying a used 3.4 and doing all the modifications necessary. Also what do I need to take off the top half of the intake<BR>plenum ? It's looks like a 12 point 10 mm socket might work. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||contra||08-12-2000||01:24 PM||||i would like to know this too because if my motor ever dies i want to know if it's cheaper or approx. the same price to get a better motor dropped in than a rebuild.<BR>good question  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-12-2000||03:49 PM||||Generally speaking, it will be about the same amount (maybe a little cheaper) to install a low mileage 3.4 than rebuilding your 2.8.  Used 3.4's can be had for $500-$1000, while the parts for a rebuild and the machine shop costs can approach that much during a rebuild.<P>The hardest part about the 3.4 is getting the starter holes drilled properly, other than that it is virtually a bolt in proposition. <P>The upper plenum is held on by 12-point 10mm bolts.||||reg||6
Z||000003||terryk||08-12-2000||06:09 PM||||I agree, if you can find a low miles 3.4L, do that.<P>This site has some good details on the starter issue.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||contra||08-12-2000||10:02 PM||||cool!<BR>i'll consider that highly when my fiero's motor goes kaput. For now it's running strong. maybe a cheap turbo would be nice for the time being  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||08-12-2000||10:29 PM||||"Cheap Turbo" is an oxymoron.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||08-13-2000||12:45 AM||||Don't forget to check this place:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm</A> <P>They have used 3.4s complete. Minus PS, A/C, etc. Come with heads, injectors, everything needed for the swap. They don't understand that an f-body engine will work in the Fiero, so just don't mention you want it for a Fiero. I have called them several times, good guys on the phone, knowledgeable,  but I haven't bought anything from them yet.||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||08-13-2000||02:29 PM||||Thanks for the link fiero56!!  I think I know where im going to buy my 3.4L Fiero motor! hahahahahaha...........3.4  power.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Of course then I will have to change my signature...<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||14
